{
  "kanji": "本",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 本\ntitle: book, origin\njlpt: 5\ntags: [jlpt-n5, grade-1, indicative, starter]\nstrokes: 5\nradical: 木\nradicalNumber: 75\nonyomi: [ホン]\nkunyomi: [もと]\ndistractors: [木, 休, 大]\n---\n\n# 本 — book, origin\n\n**Strokes:** 5 · **Key (radical):** 木 (no. 75) · **JLPT:** N5 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n本 is [木](木.md) (tree) with a short mark across the bottom of the trunk, pointing at the roots: an indicative character for \"root, base\".\nFrom \"root\" come \"origin\", \"main\", \"true, real\" and, through the sense of a basic or written source, \"book\". The step to \"book\" is explained in different ways; what is clear is that it\nis the standard word for a book in Japanese today. 本 is also a counter for long, thin objects.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ホン | on | [本](../words/本.md) ほん (book), [日本](../words/日本.md) にほん／にっぽん, 本当 ほんとう, 本物 ほんもの, 手本 てほん |\n| もと | kun | 本 もと (origin, base; rare alone), 山本 やまもと (surname), 本を正せば もとをただせば |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [本](../words/本.md) ほん — book\n- [日本](../words/日本.md) にほん — Japan\n- 本当 ほんとう — truth, real\n- 本物 ほんもの — the real thing\n- [日本刀](../words/日本刀.md) にほんとう — Japanese sword; 日本 names Japan in this compound\n\n## Notes\n\n**Counter:** 本 counts long, thin things (pencils, bottles, trains, films): the reading changes with the preceding number.\n一本 いっぽん, 二本 にほん, 三本 さんぼん, 四本 よんほん, 五本 ごほん, 六本 ろっぽん, 七本 ななほん, 八本 はっぽん／はちほん, 九本 きゅうほん, 十本 じゅっぽん／じっぽん, 何本 なんぼん.\nSo the reading cycles between ほん, ぽん and ぼん.\n\nLook-alikes: [木](木.md) (tree) has no mark at the root; 末 (end, tip) has a longer upper stroke; 未 (not yet) has a longer lower stroke.\n休 ([休](休.md)) and 体 (body) are 亻 beside 木 or 本.\n",
